.\" -------- fancyquote(1) --------
.TH FANCYQUOTE 1 "2025-08-29" "fancyquote 0.1"
.SH NAME
fancyquote \- display a centered quote in the terminal
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fancyquote
prints a centered quote inside a framed rectangle using the wide-character ncurses API,
wrapping long lines, handling multi-line input, and optionally decorating the frame with
an author banner. If no arguments are supplied, the quote is read from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B -a, --author \fIname\fR
Show \fIname\fR centered along the top border of the frame.
.TP
.B -ct, --colortext \fIcolor\fR
Render the quote text using \fIcolor\fR.
.TP
.B -cr, --colorrectangle \fIcolor\fR
Render the frame using \fIcolor\fR.
.TP
.B -ca, --colorauth \fIcolor\fR
Render the author banner using \fIcolor\fR.
.PP
Color arguments accept the standard ncurses color names (black, red, green, yellow, blue,
magenta, cyan, white) or a numeric color index that your terminal supports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
fancyquote Hello there General Kenobi
.br
printf 'It\'s over, Anakin.\nI have the high ground.' | fancyquote
.br
fancyquote -a "Obi-Wan Kenobi" -ct yellow -cr blue -ca white "Hello there"
.fi
